    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0310" n="218" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg218"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9719</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Droppers</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-26T22:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 26, 1918, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 27, 9.15 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>488. Your 429, April 19, 5 p.m. Have given publicity to statement in your
                    telegram. It has had happy and widespread effect. Venizelos said to me a month ago he would like some assurance
                    from Entente Powers about integrity of Greece, if not publicly then privately,
                    so that he could if challenged in the House of Representatives reassure the
                    members.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Droppers</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
